      "extract": "Division algebras, specifically quaternions and octonions, Jordan and related algebras, are described \\cite{key-1} in a conceited manner in unified theories of basic interactions. Quaternions were discovered by Hamilton \\cite{key-2} in 1843 as an illustration of group structure and also applied to mechanics in three-dimensional space. Quaternions have the same properties as complex numbers with the difference that",
